       return render_template('my_books.html', books=user_books, message=message)
   ```

   - Update the `my_books.html` template to display this message if applicable.

3. **Ensure Title Consistency Across Templates:**
   - Review and update the titles for UI pages to ensure consistency with expected values in the tests. In this case, the registration page should either be explicitly titled "Register" or the tests should expect "Registration." Choose a single convention and apply it throughout the application.

   ```html
   <!-- Modify the registration.html title accordingly -->
   <title>Register</title>
   ```

   - Ensure other relevant templates have consistent naming conventions for titles that are expected in the respective unit tests.

By addressing these issues, the application will not only pass the unit tests more consistently, but also provide a better overall user experience. It¡¯s important to establish clear expectations for data and responses, which will lead to improved maintainability and reliability of the code.

